1
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:24,030
Marshal,

2
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,280
they've left.

3
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,480
Do you know

4
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:33,390
why I let that ungrateful son go?

5
00:00:33,390 --> 00:00:35,280
=Cases Between Us=

6
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,880
I wouldn't presume to guess.

7
00:00:37,024 --> 00:00:39,104
=Episode 36=
I'm sure you have your reasons.

8
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:42,150
Adjutant Sun,

9
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:44,240
let me ask you something.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,880
What do you think

11
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,280
it takes to conquer the world?

12
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,710
I'm all ears.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,110
Ruthless means.

14
00:00:59,110 --> 00:01:02,350
Seize power at any cost.

15
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:04,480
Iron will.

16
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,280
Anyone in my way is expendable.

17
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:10,040
The strong always prevail.

18
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,000
As for the weak,

19
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,000
no one cares.

20
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,840
If we lose the shipment, so be it.

21
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:26,280
To me,

22
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,070
it was just a test.

23
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:32,230
I wanted to see

24
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:37,430
if my son was worthy of your efforts.

25
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:42,000
I failed you.

26
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,000
Please punish me.

27
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,710
If Yuan Hong is smart,

28
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:52,760
you two may have a real contest.

29
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,590
Then the winner

30
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:57,680
will deserve what I've built.

31
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:01,430
But if he's a fool,

32
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:05,280
then this game

33
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,030
isn't his to play.

34
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,030
Where are you going?

35
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,224
Where's your gun?

36
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,470
If my father wants a fight,

37
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:35,520
I'll fight him to the end.

38
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:53,630
Wan'er.

39
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,000
How did it go?

40
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,190
Did you hand everything over?

41
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,150
The thumb ring and the shipment
are with the police now.

42
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:00,430
Good.

43
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,680
Father should be fine now.

44
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,000
Who's he?

45
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,080
Kobayashi's driver.

46
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,400
We questioned him all night.

47
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:08,120
According to him,

48
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,870
Kobayashi is escorting

49
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:11,360
a ship loaded with methamphetamine

50
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:12,590
to Dagu Port tonight.

51
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,800
Methamphetamine?

52
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,750
This is

53
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:16,840
its clinical trial report.

54
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,120
Dr. Du got it for me.

55
00:03:18,352 --> 00:03:19,710
They claim it boosts alertness,

56
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,280
but it's no different from opium.

57
00:03:21,408 --> 00:03:22,430
It's even worse than that.

58
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:23,000
Exactly.

59
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:25,280
The Japanese Army planned to use it,

60
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,150
but they feared the side effects.

61
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:28,520
So Kobayashi brought it to China

62
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,630
to test it on civilians.

63
00:03:29,696 --> 00:03:31,240
Using the Chinese as human guinea pigs.

64
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,520
Just last month, in North China alone,

65
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,240
this drug drove

66
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,870
over a hundred people insane.

67
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,680
Those monsters.

68
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,710
We have to stop this operation.

69
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,000
Kobayashi works with your father.

70
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,240
At a time like this,

71
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,520
he lets you go.

72
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,590
Don't you think it's a trap?

73
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:50,030
Even if it costs me my life,

74
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,190
I'll break it.

75
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,710
Don't talk nonsense.

76
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,080
Wan'er,

77
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,510
call every reporter you can.

78
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,630
The more, the better.

79
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:00,150
Force the government to act.

80
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:00,870
Only then

81
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,470
can we all make it out alive.

82
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,960
We're counting on you all.

83
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:09,030
- No problem.
- You got it.

84
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:09,960
No problem.

85
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,560
We'll back each other up.

86
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,600
Time's tight. There are
only three major papers.

87
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,800
The rest are tabloids.

88
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,870
That's enough.

89
00:04:27,616 --> 00:04:29,008
Once it's over, write it up.

90
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:31,750
Get it in print as soon as possible.
Don't give the Japanese time to react.

91
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:32,480
Got it.

92
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:43,270
This will be a tough fight.

93
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,390
Don't worry.

94
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:46,360
I don't wear this uniform to look cool.

95
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:57,390
Commissioner...

96
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,070
Quite the operation.

97
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,190
Anti-smuggling?

98
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,800
That's Customs' job.

99
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:12,070
What has it got to do with you?

100
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:14,120
And you, too.

101
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,630
Pack it up.

102
00:05:16,310 --> 00:05:17,240
The Japanese

103
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,480
are about to flood China

104
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,190
with a new narcotic.

105
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:21,680
You're just going to watch?

106
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,360
Commissioner,

107
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,560
have you chosen

108
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,720
to side with the Japanese?

109
00:05:26,870 --> 00:05:27,750
You two,

110
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,950
quit acting like big shots.

111
00:05:30,950 --> 00:05:33,120
With those few guns,

112
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:35,680
you think you can beat a warship?

113
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,480
And you too.

114
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,920
Why get dragged into this?

115
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,950
Fall back.

116
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:43,360
Listen up!

117
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:46,360
All officers, withdraw immediately!

118
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,480
Anyone who disobeys

119
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,920
hands in their uniforms and leaves.

120
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,270
None of you is moving?

121
00:06:24,690 --> 00:06:26,500
Something's happening at the dock.
Turn around.

122
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:27,190
Yes, sir.

123
00:06:35,870 --> 00:06:36,510
This is bad.

124
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:37,510
The ship's turning back.

125
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,070
Yang Dezhi.

126
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,680
Think about your family. Be sensible.

127
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,120
Don't throw your life away
with those two idiots.

128
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:49,240
Everyone else,

129
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,070
fall back!

130
00:06:51,830 --> 00:06:52,480
Move!

131
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:09,600
Sir, I need to borrow your boat.

132
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:42,950
Who's there?

133
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:46,390
Go check it out! Hurry!

134
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:02,750
What are you doing?

135
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:03,870
Find a weapon.

136
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:40,960
The enemy is here!

137
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:06,870
They're over here!

138
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,600
Send reinforcements!

139
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,440
Found one!

140
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,150
This is it.

141
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:23,390
It's like ice.

142
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,790
Commander Yuan.

143
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,390
Mr. Zhao.

144
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:31,120
We meet again.

145
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:33,550
Commander Yuan,

146
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,200
think this through.

147
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:38,240
That shipment belongs to your father.

148
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,750
It can buy plenty of guns

149
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:41,440
and plenty of cannons.

150
00:10:41,790 --> 00:10:43,910
If you ruin this deal,

151
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:45,390
your father's empire

152
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,750
will be shaken to its core.

153
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
He's him.

154
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,390
What has that got to do with me?

155
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,390
Do you know

156
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:58,270
the consequences of crossing
the Imperial Japanese Army?

157
00:10:59,240 --> 00:10:59,750
Do you know

158
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:01,584
the consequences of
dealing drugs in China?

159
00:11:01,728 --> 00:11:03,150
The shore is full of reporters.

160
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,000
Your crimes will soon be exposed.

161
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,390
Exposed?

162
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:10,390
So what?

163
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:16,000
When your mother died,

164
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,270
even your father had to swallow it.

165
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,910
Now it's your turn.

166
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,030
You'll swallow it, too.

167
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,480
Plan C.

168
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:04,480
Execute!

169
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:08,150
Zhao Shaoshang!

170
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,080
Zhao Shaoshang!

171
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,080
Zhao Shaoshang!

172
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,390
Happy now?

173
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:31,550
You killed my mother.

174
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:33,510
Now Zhao Shaoshang is dead, too.

175
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:35,670
Everyone who mattered to me is gone.

176
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,270
And now,

177
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,270
how many more shipments of weapons

178
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:41,630
will you trade him to the Japanese for?

179
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:47,080
Your arrogance got him killed.

180
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:49,440
How is that my fault?

181
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:57,510
You're about to die,

182
00:13:58,030 --> 00:14:00,030
and you still won't repent.

183
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:07,840
About to die?

184
00:14:11,550 --> 00:14:13,670
Do you know how

185
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:15,550
I built this empire?

186
00:14:16,304 --> 00:14:17,776
Two stab wounds to my left chest

187
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:21,200
fighting the British.

188
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,790
A bullet through my back

189
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:25,670
during the warlord conflicts.

190
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:26,870
I survived them all.

191
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:29,840
You think I'll die by your hand?

192
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:41,790
I endured humiliation

193
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:43,080
and made every compromise.

194
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,510
For what?

195
00:14:44,510 --> 00:14:46,240
Wasn't it all for you?

196
00:14:47,150 --> 00:14:49,200
And what did you do?

197
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,480
Not only are you ungrateful,

198
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,550
but you also pointed a gun at me
for an outsider.

199
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,550
What an ungrateful son I have raised.

200
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,270
You want to shoot me?

201
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,240
Aim right here.

202
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,360
Right here!

203
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,120
Go on!

204
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:09,630
Let's see what you've got.

205
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:15,270
Even now,

206
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,150
you still don't know

207
00:15:18,150 --> 00:15:19,960
what you did wrong.

208
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:23,440
You're

209
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,270
just like your mother.

210
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:29,870
I never

211
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:32,030
should have

212
00:15:32,030 --> 00:15:34,000
sent you to live with her.

213
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:35,840
A narrow-minded woman

214
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,360
raises children

215
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:40,750
who are just as indecisive.

216
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:44,080
To toughen you up,

217
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,510
I sent you to a military academy.

218
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:50,840
You did become a little tougher.

219
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,480
Who would've thought you would end up

220
00:15:56,544 --> 00:15:59,088
hanging around with a spoiled brat?

221
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,200
Can you really not tell what matters?

222
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:06,120
Or are you

223
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,080
so blinded by loyalty

224
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,270
that you've tied your own hands?

225
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:21,670
It's just one Zhao Shaoshang.

226
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:25,200
You're not worthy of being my son.

227
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,400
(February 2, before dawn,
the Marshal's camp was attacked.)

228
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,650
(Zhao Chengru resigned and left Beijing
with the recovered Tong Mengling.)

229
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:49,630
(Zhao Wan'er launched a Ta Kung Pao
column to expose the truth of the times.)

230
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:51,450
(Yang Dezhi succeeded as Chief of
the Police Department's Division Four.)

231
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:53,450
(Zhao Shaoshang vanished into the sea,
and everyone believed he had died.)

232
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:54,660
(But the storm was far from over...)

233
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:56,840
(Yuan Hong...)

234
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,030
(Wan'er...)

235
00:16:58,790 --> 00:17:00,080
(Everyone thought I was dead.)

236
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,720
(Even I )

237
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,480
(thought I wouldn't survive.)

238
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,590
(But a passing Japanese merchant ship)

239
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:07,790
(pulled me out of the water.)

240
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:11,880
Who is this?

241
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,240
No idea.

242
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,070
My, my.

243
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:44,240
Where on earth am I?

244
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:56,420
(Nagasaki Port)

245
00:18:56,820 --> 00:19:00,660
(End of Episode 36)

246
00:19:01,801 --> 00:19:03,441
♪Side by side,
we journey through this life♪

247
00:19:03,441 --> 00:19:04,981
♪Troubled times
are but a laughing matter♪

248
00:19:04,981 --> 00:19:06,231
♪However, the world changes♪

249
00:19:06,231 --> 00:19:08,151
♪You'll still be by my side♪

250
00:19:08,151 --> 00:19:09,841
♪Side by side,
we journey through this life♪

251
00:19:09,841 --> 00:19:11,411
♪Praise and blame come and go♪

252
00:19:11,411 --> 00:19:12,981
♪If this is my final chapter♪

253
00:19:12,981 --> 00:19:15,481
♪I'll solve this mystery with you♪
